From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Mckeever <ryan.mckeever@collabora.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 15:31:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pan/bi: set branch reconvergence at loop exit points

A clause requires reconvergence if it has a successor that can be executed
without first executing the clause itself. Separate iterations of a loop
are treated separately here. So when the loop iteration count is not
warp-invariant, we need branch reconvergence at loop exit points.

This commit is setting reconvergence for all loop exit points, so we could
do better by checking if the loop is warp-invariant.

Reviewed-by: Lorenzo Rossi <lorenzo.rossi@collabora.com>
Reviewed-by: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/41981>
(cherry picked from commit 8b03ae787f43edc6ea2e94952d68d81221770082)
---
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost/bi_schedule.c | 3 ++-
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c     | 6 ++++++
 src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/compiler.h            | 3 +++
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost/bi_schedule.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost/bi_schedule.c
index c655956afae..070179d8617 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost/bi_schedule.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost/bi_schedule.c
@@ -2017,7 +2017,8 @@ bi_schedule_block(bi_context *ctx, bi_block *block)
    if (!list_is_empty(&block->clauses)) {
       bi_clause *last_clause =
          list_last_entry(&block->clauses, bi_clause, link);
-      if (bi_reconverge_branches(block))
+      if (bi_reconverge_branches(block) ||
+          block->needs_reconvergence_on_exit)
          last_clause->flow_control = BIFROST_FLOW_NBTB_UNCONDITIONAL;
    }
 
diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
index d3ec0ccb16b..28bf6ea91af 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bifrost_compile.c
@@ -89,6 +89,12 @@ bi_emit_jump(bi_builder *b, nir_jump_instr *instr)
    switch (instr->type) {
    case nir_jump_break:
       branch->branch_target = b->shader->break_block;
+
+      /* We need branch reconvergence in the break block of a loop unless
+       * the loop is warp-invariant.
+       * TODO: check for warp-invariance
+       */
+      b->shader->current_block->needs_reconvergence_on_exit = true;
       break;
    case nir_jump_continue:
       branch->branch_target = b->shader->continue_block;
diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/compiler.h b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/compiler.h
index 95a012db0b3..8495f827583 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/compiler.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/compiler.h
@@ -970,6 +970,9 @@ typedef struct bi_block {
    bool unconditional_jumps;
    bool loop_header;
 
+   /* whether this is a loop exit point that needs branch reconvergence */
+   bool needs_reconvergence_on_exit;
+
    /* Per 32-bit word live masks for the block indexed by node */
    uint8_t *live_in;
    uint8_t *live_out;
